Package: hexmakR
Title: Editable Hex Stickers and Project Logos
Version: 0.3.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("R.", "Heller", , "raban.heller@uni-ulm.de",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8006-9742")),
    person("The JetBrains Mono Project Authors", role = "cph",
           comment = "JetBrains Mono font")
  )
Description: Create publication-ready hexagon stickers for R packages
    interactively via a 'shiny' app or programmatically via R functions.
    Complements the 'hexSticker' package (which embeds R plots into
    stickers) by providing an interactive visual designer with 28 curated
    colour themes (dark and light variants, led by the nine families of the
    Computational Trauma and Tissue Injury Research (CTTIR) design, version
    5 (CTTIR v5)), 46 built-in scientific and technical icons, custom image
    upload support, font selection, and export to transparent PNG. Designed
    for the R package ecosystem with presets for CRAN, Bioconductor,
    Tidyverse, and domain-specific colour palettes. Includes the CTTIR v5
    library of 45 native R vector identities, editable shapes, reproducible
    JSON projects, and transparent PNG, SVG and PDF export with package
    names inside the hexagon. Project logos also support pentagonal and
    square frames.
